<Prose
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What data PB&B collects, why, and what control you have over it."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  standfirst="What we collect, why we collect it, and how to get it removed."
  updated="[CONFIRM] date"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers pbnb.store. The data controller is
    <mark class="todo">[FILL] registered business name and contact address</mark>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Order information</strong> — name, email, shipping and billing address, phone number
      if you give one, and what you bought. We need this to fulfil the order.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment information</strong> — handled by Shopify's checkout. We receive confirmation
      that payment succeeded and the last four digits of the card. We never see or store your full
      card number.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your bag</strong> — a cookie holding an identifier for your shopping bag so it
      survives between page loads. It contains no personal information.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Marketing</strong> — your email address, if you sign up for drop announcements.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data</strong> — your IP address is forwarded to Shopify with product and
      cart requests. Shopify uses it for fraud and bot protection and to keep one shopper's traffic
      from affecting another's. It is not used to profile you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>We don't sell your data, and we don't share it with advertisers.</p>

  <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Shopify</strong> — store backend, checkout, payments and order records.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting and delivery of this site.</li>
    <li><strong>Shipping carriers</strong> — the name and address needed to deliver your parcel.</li>
    <li><mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> Any email marketing or analytics tool you add, e.g. Klaviyo.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We set a cookie for your shopping bag, which is required for the store to work. Shopify sets its
    own cookies during checkout for the same reason.
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> whether any analytics or marketing cookies are added — if so,
    a consent banner is required in the UK/EU and this section needs to list them.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Order records are kept for as long as tax and accounting law requires
    (<mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] typically 6–7 years</mark>). Marketing emails are kept until you
    unsubscribe.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Depending on
    where you live you may also have the right to object to processing or to data portability
    (GDPR), or to opt out of sale or sharing (CCPA — we do neither). Email
    <a href="/contact">support</a> and we'll respond within 30 days.
  </p>
  <p>You can unsubscribe from marketing at any time with the link in any email.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This store isn't directed at children under 13 and we don't knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes materially we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
</Prose>
